### 2. Why Android is Fast
The Android implementation in [PlatformPdfParser.kt](file:///Users/sunil/Downloads/PDFParser/shared/src/androidMain/kotlin/com/ssbmax/pdfparser/parser/PdfParser.kt) utilizes Apache PDFBox (`pdfbox-android`):

```kotlin
private class SpatialTextStripper(...) : PDFTextStripper() {
    override fun writeString(
        text: String?,
        textPositions: MutableList<TextPosition>?,
    ) {
        ...
        for (tp in textPositions) {
            val cx = tp.xDirAdj
            val cy = tp.yDirAdj
            ...
        }
    }
}
```

* **No Per-Character API Queries:** PDFBox processes the raw PDF binary streams sequentially and provides the pre-computed character coordinates directly as a list of `TextPosition` objects in `writeString`.
* **Zero Interop Boundary Crossings:** The loop iterates over local JVM objects. There are no JNI boundary crossings or layout search queries happening per character in the processing loop.

