### 3. How to Optimize the iOS App

If you want to speed up the iOS parsing time, you can implement one of these optimization strategies:

#### Option A: Word-Level Scan (e.g., reduces parsing time to ~1–2 seconds)
Instead of querying bounds for every single character, extract words (consecutive sequences of non-whitespace characters) first. This reduces the number of layout and interop calls by **5x to 8x** (the average length of a word).

```kotlin
// Example optimization approach in extractTextSpatially
val words = findWordRanges(pageString) // Local parsing to group indices of words
for (range in words) {
    val selection = page.selectionForRange(range) ?: continue
    val rectVal = selection.boundsForPage(page)
    // Map the word's bounding box to the characters inside it
}
```

#### Option B: Low-Level CoreGraphics Parsing
Instead of using `PDFKit`, utilize `CGPDFPage` and configure a `CGPDFScanner` with a `CGPDFOperatorTable` in CoreGraphics. This allows you to register callbacks for text layout operators (like `Tj` or `TJ`) to retrieve characters and coordinates directly from the PDF stream in a single pass at native speeds.

